<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monza</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Monza is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, just north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. It was a residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodelinda">Theodelinda</a>, whose cathedral holds the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-crown-of-lombardy">Iron Crown of Lombardy</a>, and its royal villa was a summer residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-savoy">House of Savoy</a>. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umberto-i">Umberto I</a> was assassinated there by the anarchist Gaetano Bresci on 29 July 1900.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monza.jpg" alt="Monza" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Bonacina · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reggia_di_Monza.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
